% composition-bridge: Listen for how a contemporary hip-hop track controls conversational timing, rhyme placement, space and changes of vocal register inside a repeating production frame.
% composition-context: TOBi is a Nigerian-born, Brampton-raised Canadian rapper and singer. The artist-uploaded track is categorized as hip-hop/rap and was released in September 2026.
% composition-distance: Original classroom-safe words, D-minor hook, body-percussion ostinato and chord loop; no flow, lyric, beat, sample, melody or production element from TOBi's recording is used.
% improv: {"id":"A","bars":"5-8","role":"solo or pair","prompt":"Complete the two-bar thought","choices":["straight eighth flow","triplet flow","speak only on beats 2 and 4"],"replyBars":4}
% improv: {"id":"B","bars":"13-16","role":"producer/conductor","prompt":"Choose the hook arrangement","choices":["all layers in","voice and bass only","drop one bar then return"],"replyBars":4}
% dossier-function: original Grade 6 alternative-hip-hop cypher bridge; the class maintains a four-bar ostinato, pairs write and perform a two-bar answer under clear content rules, and a conductor chooses the final drop and return
% dossier-elements: sixteen bars in 4/4 with one sung pickup eighth after an eighth rest; D-minor hook D-F-G-A with C sharp on the A-major V, D4-A4 range; straight eighths, eighth-note triplets and syncopated rests; Dm-Gm-A (i-iv-V); layered body percussion, spoken rhythm and sung hook; verse/hook AABA form
% dossier-practice: Rehearsal key D minor; written hook range D4-A4, with spoken verses adaptable to any comfortable voice. Quarter note = 88. Establish the kick-pat on beats 1 and 3 and clap on 2 and 4, speak the pickup, compare one bar of straight eighths with one of triplets, then write only two bars. Offer beat-making, conducting or instrumental roles instead of public rapping.
% dossier-accompaniment: Newly authored Dm-Gm-A loop, bass roots and classroom body percussion. No copyrighted sample and no attempt to copy TOBi's beat. A digital version may use only licensed or student-recorded sounds whose provenance is documented.
% dossier-lyrics: Original English hook and verse frame. Student verses must follow class-agreed boundaries: no personal disclosures required, no insults, slurs or naming classmates, and anyone may pass. Record student authorship and consent before saving text.
% dossier-honesty: AI-assisted original composition, 11 November 2026; not by TOBi, not freestyle evidence and not a transcription or imitation. The reference teaches listening and craft.
% dossier-licence: CC0 1.0 for the supplied hook, verse frame, harmony and ABC. Student verses retain student authorship unless separately and knowingly licensed; TOBi's work remains copyrighted.
% dossier-respect: Teach hip-hop as a Black cultural practice with histories of DJing, MCing, dance, visual art, community testimony and technological invention. Do not frame rap as merely speaking over a beat or require stereotyped delivery.
% dossier-review: Grade 6 teacher, hip-hop educator, second score reader, privacy/accessibility reviewer and student cypher trial; all reviews still required
