N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): The score starts with one sung pickup eighth after an eighth rest. Every full bar totals eight eighth units. Bars 1-4 are the sung hook; bars 5-8 provide notated straight, triplet and offbeat models for replacing with a student two-bar thought; bars 9-12 return to the hook; bars 13-16 repeat it under the live arrangement choice. Pitch set D-E-F-G-A with C sharp on the A chord, range D4-A4.
N:UNCERTAIN: Student comfort, authorship workflow, text safety, whether the triplet notation reads cleanly and whether the groove supports rather than crowds speech require specialist and classroom trials.
